All edits are applied to `system/app.js` and the file passes `node --check` (syntax clean). Summary of what changed:

Added `icon()` and `iconHtml()` helpers that build `<svg class="icon"><use href="#i-…"/></svg>` via `createElementNS` so the air-gapped sprite resolves with no network request. Extended `TABS` with a third icon-name element and rewrote `buildTabs()` to append an icon plus a `<span class="tab-label">` per button, preserving each button's exact text content while adding `type="button"` and `title`. `show()` now writes the active workspace label into `#pageTitle`, and a reusable `pageHeader(title, subtitle)` builder (exposing `.actions`) was added and inserted as the first node in all six view builders. Wired the `#sidebarToggle` collapse toggle in `boot()` with `wvn_sidebar_collapsed` persistence and `aria-expanded` updates, and made `setTheme()` swap the theme button's innerHTML between the sun/moon sprite icons.

Converted every rendered glyph to its sprite equivalent: `⚠`→`alert-triangle`, `💬`→`message-circle`, `📂`→`folder-open`, `✎`→`pencil`, `→`→`arrow-right`, and the expand/collapse triangles (`▲`/`▼`/`&#9660;`/`&#9654;`)→`chevron-down`/`chevron-right` across the step-card toggle, note-thread toggles, and LFI caret. Glyphs sitting inside `alert()` strings, comments, `title` attributes, and `<option value="…">` attributes were intentionally left as plain text since an SVG cannot render there. `node --check` confirms the file still parses, and the `#tabs` button label strings remain byte-for-byte unchanged for the test suite.
